{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775510932,"nonce":"PCtz+Q8CZkHENWqfPR1VT5XpI50=","title":"Ship nightshift MCP signal server in Docker image","message":"Ship nightshift MCP signal server in Docker image\n\n## Context\nSignal protocol Phase 1: ship the MCP server that exposes nightshift_done, nightshift_checkpoint, and nightshift_question tools. Tested working with Claude Code and Codex (see docs/signal-protocol-design.md). This issue only creates and bundles the server — adapter integration is separate.\n\n## Tests (write first, must fail before implementation)\n- tests/test_mcp_signal_server.py::test_initialize_returns_protocol_version\n  Assert: sending initialize request returns protocolVersion \"2024-11-05\" and serverInfo name \"nightshift-signals\"\n- tests/test_mcp_signal_server.py::test_tools_list_returns_three_tools\n  Assert: tools/list returns exactly 3 tools: nightshift_done, nightshift_checkpoint, nightshift_question\n- tests/test_mcp_signal_server.py::test_tools_call_done_returns_signal\n  Assert: calling nightshift_done with summary arg returns content with \"Signal received: nightshift_done\"\n- tests/test_mcp_signal_server.py::test_tools_call_checkpoint_returns_signal\n  Assert: calling nightshift_checkpoint with description arg returns signal acknowledgment\n- tests/test_mcp_signal_server.py::test_tools_call_question_returns_signal\n  Assert: calling nightshift_question with question arg returns signal acknowledgment\n- tests/test_mcp_signal_server.py::test_unknown_method_returns_error\n  Assert: unknown method returns JSON-RPC error -32601\n- tests/test_mcp_signal_server.py::test_notifications_initialized_returns_none\n  Assert: notifications/initialized returns no response (notification, not request)\n\n## Files\n- nightshift-mcp-server.py (create — MCP stdio server)\n- mcp-config.json (create — config pointing to the server script)\n- Dockerfile (modify — COPY both files to /opt/nightshift/)\n\n## Implementation\n1. Create `nightshift-mcp-server.py`: JSON-RPC 2.0 stdio server implementing MCP protocol.\n   - `initialize` → returns protocolVersion \"2024-11-05\", capabilities {tools: {}}, serverInfo {name: \"nightshift-signals\", version: \"1.0.0\"}\n   - `notifications/initialized` → return None (no response for notifications)\n   - `tools/list` → returns 3 tools:\n     - nightshift_done(summary: str) — \"Signal that the task is complete\"\n     - nightshift_checkpoint(description: str) — \"Signal a checkpoint with progress description\"  \n     - nightshift_question(question: str) — \"Ask a question and wait for an answer\"\n   - `tools/call` → logs signal to stderr, returns acknowledgment text\n   - Unknown methods → JSON-RPC error -32601\n   - Reads stdin line-by-line, writes JSON responses to stdout\n2. Create `mcp-config.json`:\n   ```json\n   {\"mcpServers\": {\"nightshift-signals\": {\"command\": \"python3\", \"args\": [\"/opt/nightshift/nightshift-mcp-server.py\"]}}}\n   ```\n3. Update Dockerfile: add `COPY nightshift-mcp-server.py /opt/nightshift/` and `COPY mcp-config.json /opt/nightshift/`\n\n## Patterns to follow\nSee /tmp/nightshift-mcp-server-v2.py for the tested prototype (docs/signal-protocol-design.md references it).\nSee docs/signal-protocol-design.md \"MCP Server\" section for the JSON-RPC protocol.\n\nREQ: REQ-004","files":null}]}